  1 | /**
  2 |  * \file validation_session.hpp
  3 |  * \brief Standalone C++20 foundation for an explicit time authority, an immutable
  4 |  *        local validation permit, and a bounded validation-session lifecycle.
  5 |  *
  6 |  * \details
  7 |  * This header belongs to the source-free T025 engineering candidate of
  8 |  * `xverse::xcom::validation`. It uses only the C++20 standard library and includes no
  9 |  * predecessor header. It defines no communication item, transport, gateway, network
 10 |  * listener, journal, lease, dashboard, persistent store, or external-service surface, and
 11 |  * every nominal code path is free of file, socket, and environment I/O.
 12 |  *
 13 |  * The three cooperating components are:
 14 |  * - `TimeAuthority` — declared clock domains, bounded current-time reads, and directed
 15 |  *   source-to-destination mappings with a live tolerance cross-check.
 16 |  * - `Permit` / `PermitBuilder` — an immutable envelope binding exactly one session
 17 |  *   identity and its full operational context, with a deterministic FNV-1a content
 18 |  *   identity and a closed allowed-action set.
 19 |  * - `SessionManager` — controller identity/generation, exactly-once consumption, bounded
 20 |  *   live-session capacity, and the validation-session lifecycle state machine.
 21 |  *
 22 |  * \note This is an internal candidate. It does not establish accepted X-COM delivery,
 23 |  *       predecessor regression, source compatibility, protected verification, or
 24 |  *       production readiness.
 25 |  */
